    "q-100839": {
      "dom_id": "step-q100839",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the general formula for the $n$th term of the arithmetic sequence that begins with \n\n$$\n19,\\,17,\\,15,\\,…\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nFrom the first few terms\n\n$$\n19,\\,17,\\,15,\\,…\n$$\n\nwe see that the first term is $f(1)=19$ and the common difference is \n\n$$\nd=17-19=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =19+(n-1)(-2) \\\\  & =19-2n+2 \\\\  & =21-2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is $f(n)=21-2n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
